    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine the domain and range of $f\\circ f$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Domain $(1,\\infty)$; range $\\mathbb R$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ f)(x)&=\\log_2(\\log_2x)\\end{align*}$$\nThe outer logarithm requires $\\log_2x>0$, which gives $x>1$. As $x$ runs through $(1,\\infty)$, $\\log_2x$ runs through $(0,\\infty)$, and its logarithm runs through $\\mathbb R$. Thus the domain is $(1,\\infty)$ and the range is $\\mathbb R$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Determine the domain and range of the function $f\\circ f\\circ\\cdots\\circ f$ obtained by composing $n$ copies of $f$, where $n>2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Domain $(k_n,\\infty)$; range $\\mathbb R$, where $k_2=1$ and $k_{m+1}=2^{k_m}$.\n\nFor $n>2$, $k_n$ is a tower of $n-2$ copies of $2$, with exponentiation evaluated from the top.",
          "worked": "Write $F_n$ for the composition of $n$ copies of $f$. From part (a), the domain threshold is $k_2=1$.\nThe identity $F_{m+1}(x)=F_m(\\log_2x)$ shows that its domain requires\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2x&>k_m\\\\x&>2^{k_m}\\end{align*}$$\nThus $k_{m+1}=2^{k_m}$. In particular, $k_3=2$, $k_4=2^2=4$, and $k_5=2^{2^2}=16$. For $n>2$, $k_n$ is a tower containing $n-2$ copies of $2$.\nOn $(k_n,\\infty)$, the repeated logarithm is continuous and increasing, tends to $-\\infty$ as $x\\to k_n^+$ and tends to $+\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty$. Therefore its domain is $(k_n,\\infty)$ and its range is $\\mathbb R$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
